Free fund switches (Equity to Debt) ULIP me bina koi Capital Gain Tax diye market time karne ka fayda deta hai?

Budget 2021 tax update: 2.5 Lakh se zyada annual premium wale ULIPs ab Section 10(10D) tax-free maturity nahi dete (LTCG 12.5% lagega)?

ULIP me "Return of Mortality Charges" (ROMC) feature maturity par cover cost wapas kar deta hai, iska real math (time value of money)?

Top-up premium in ULIPs: Extra surplus paise ko existig ULIP fund me add karne ka tax-free benefit?

NAV (Net Asset Value) calculation ULIPs me mutual funds se alag hoti hai ya totally same (daily pricing)?

Death benefit in ULIP: Sum Insured ya Fund Value (jo bhi higher ho) nominee ko milta hai (Type I vs Type II ULIP).

Type II ULIP me death hone par nominee ko Sum Insured + Fund Value (Dono) milta hai, iska premium zyada kyu hota hai?

Partial withdrawal 5 saal lock-in khatam hone ke baad tax-free nikal sakte hain (maximum 20% of fund value)?

Pension Plans (Annuity) kya hote hain aur retirement corpus ko regular income me kaise convert karte hain?

Deferred Annuity vs Immediate Annuity me farak kya hai retirement planning ke time?

Immediate Annuity lene ke agle hi mahine se pension shuru ho jati hai (Single premium dekar).

"Annuity for life with Return of Purchase Price" (ROPP): Pension aati rahegi aur death pe original amount nominee ko wapas mil jayega.

ROPP annuity me pension yield (e.g. 6%) bina ROPP wali annuity (e.g. 8%) se kyu kam milti hai?

NPS (National Pension System) vs Insurance Company Annuity: NPS mature hone pe 40% amount mandatory annuity me daalna padta hai.

Annuity income tax free hoti hai ya salary ki tarah regular tax slab pe tax hoti hai? (Fully Taxable).

Section 80C me life insurance premium (Endowment/ULIP/Term) 1.5 Lakh tak tax exemption.

Section 80CCC pension plans aur annuity premiums contribution limit (Clubbed with 80C).

Section 80D Mediclaim premium 25,000 (Self) + 50,000 (Senior Citizen Parents) total 75,000 tax deduction.

Section 80D preventive health check-up (₹5000) cash pay karne pe bhi ITR me claim hota hai?

Section 80DDB specific critical illnesses (cancer/neurological) ke ilaaj pe 40,000 to 1 Lakh extra tax deduction.

Section 80U (Disabled person) aur 80DD (Disabled dependent) tax cover deductions for medical care and insurance maintenance.

Section 10(10D) of Income Tax Act: Life insurance maturity/death claim proceeds entirely tax-free (subject to conditions).

Traditional Endowment policies (issued post April 2023) with aggregate premium > ₹5 Lakh annually are now taxable on maturity (except death).

Keyman Insurance tax: Premium paid is business expense (Sec 37), claim payout is taxable as business income.

Group Medical Insurance premium paid by employer is treated as tax-free perquisite for employee?

GST on Health Insurance (18%) and ULIPs (18%) kya 80D / 80C deduction total amount (Premium + GST) pe calculate hota hai? (Yes).

HUF (Hindu Undivided Family) apne Karta ya members ki life insurance aur health premium bharke alag 80C/80D claim kar sakti hai.

NRI purchasing ULIP or Endowment in India: Maturity repatriable under FEMA NRO to NRE transfer rules (USD 1 Million limit).

DTAA (Double Tax Avoidance Agreement): UK/US NRI ke liye India me tax-free maturity waha ki government tax kar sakti hai?

Child Education Plans (Child ULIPs / Traditional): Waiver of premium rider inbuilt hota hai ki father ki death pe aage ki EMIs company bharegi.

Child plan me maturity bachhe ki age (18 ya 21) se sync karke withdrawal milestones (18th, 19th, 20th year) set karte hain.

Accidental Total and Permanent Disability (ATPD) rider definition: Loss of two limbs/eyes. Agar ek hath kate to kya partial payout milta hai?

Critical Illness (CI) rider me 36 bimariyan cover hoti hain (Heart attack, Stroke, Cancer). Claim ke liye 30-day survival period kyu mandatory hai?

Cancer-specific insurance vs Critical illness plan: Cancer plan early stage (Carcinoma in situ) pe bhi 20-25% payout deta hai.

Critical Illness policy premium age ke sath badhta hai (yearly renewable) ya term plan ki tarah level (fixed) rehta hai?

Women specific critical illness plans (Breast cancer, cervical cancer) aur maternity complication covers.

Hospital Cash rider (e.g. ₹2000 per day cash for expenses not covered by mediclaim) ICU admit hone pe double (₹4000) kyu ho jata hai?

Surgical benefit rider: Specific surgery (e.g. bypass) hone pe ek lumpsum fixed amount (irrespective of actual bill) milna.

Income benefit rider on disability: Pura sum insured lumpsum na dekar 1% sum insured monthly 10 saal tak dena (income replacement).

Saral Jeevan Bima: IRDAI mandated standard term insurance (5 Lakh to 25 Lakh) jisme exclusions sabhi companies ke liye strictly same hain.

Bima Kiran / Bima Jyoti guaranteed traditional plans me IRR calculation ko lock-in karna falling interest rate regime me.

Guaranteed Additions (GA) aur Loyalty Additions (LA) LIC policies me end of the term pe compounding boost kaise dete hain.

LIC policies (Par plans) sovereign guarantee back karti hai (Section 37 of LIC Act), yani govt of India ensures payout, private me nahi.

Reversionary bonus accrued har saal declare hota hai but encash maturity ya death pe hi ho sakta hai (time value loss).

Policy surrender process: Surrender value formula = (Paid up value + accrued bonus) * Surrender Value Factor (SVF).

Special Surrender Value (SSV) vs Guaranteed Surrender Value (GSV): Private life insurers SSV ko market rates ke hisab se kaise manipulate karte the (IRDAI intervened).

Policy loan at 9-10%: Surrender value ka max 90% loan milta hai. Agar loan interest aur principal surrender value cross kar jaye to policy auto-foreclose.

Micro-insurance tax-free limit: Chhoti policies rural India me tax radar se bahar rehti hain distribution friction kam karne ke liye.

ULIP taxation grand-fathering clause (policies issued before 1 Feb 2021 remain tax-free regardless of 2.5L limit).

Aggregation rule for ULIP taxation: Multiple ULIPs total premium combined to check the 2.5L threshold.

Section 112A (10% LTCG on stocks) ULIPs pe tab lagta hai jab wo equity oriented fund me invest kare aur 2.5L premium limit cross kare.

GST waiver on pure term insurance vs GST input credit on employer-sponsored term life for employees.

TDS under Section 194DA: If life insurance maturity is taxable, 5% TDS is deducted on the income component (Maturity - Premium paid).

TDS is not deducted if the total payout is less than ₹1 Lakh in a financial year.

Section 80D deduction limitation: Payment must be made by non-cash modes (UPI/Card/Cheque) to claim health insurance deduction.

Cash payment for preventive health checkup (₹5,000) is the only exception where cash is allowed under 80D.

Premium paid for parents-in-law is NOT eligible for Section 80D deduction, only parents, self, spouse, kids.

Section 80C benefit reversal: If traditional life insurance policy is terminated/surrendered within 2 years, old tax deductions are treated as current year income.

ULIP lock-in tax reversal: Surrendering ULIP before 5 years reverses all previously claimed 80C deductions.

Employer provided health insurance top-up (Super top-up paid by employee out of pocket) is eligible for 80D.

Split premium structure in endowment + health combo products: Tax department requires clear breakup to claim 80C and 80D separately.

Assignment of life policy to a trust (Estate planning) to bypass inheritance tax (if introduced in India) and protect from creditors.

Unit-linked Pension Plan (ULPP): Pension accumulation phase in market-linked funds, but vesting phase forces 1/3rd lumpsum and 2/3rd annuity.

Commutation of pension (Withdrawing a lumpsum up to 1/3rd or 60% in NPS at retirement age tax-free).

Survival benefit in Money Back policies (getting 20% sum assured every 5 years) is completely tax-free under 10(10D).

Participating policy yield drags: Traditional plans invest heavily in G-Secs (IRDAI norm 50%+ in govt bonds), capping maximum IRR at 5-6%.

Sum Assured multiplier rule: For a 1 Lakh premium, Sum Assured must be 10 Lakh (10X) to be a valid life insurance for tax-free maturity; if 5X, it is taxed.

Single premium policy trap: Giving 10 Lakh one time, getting 12.5 Lakh SA (1.25X) means the maturity will be fully taxable.

Senior citizen tax planning: Investing in immediate annuity gives fixed 7-8% return but fully taxable, comparing post-tax yield with SCSS.

Non-resident alien (USA) taxation on Indian ULIPs: PFIC (Passive Foreign Investment Company) rules making Indian ULIPs a tax nightmare for US citizens.

Endowment policy loan interest payment is NOT eligible for Section 80C or Section 24b deductions (unlike home/education loan interest).

Surrender vs Paid-up vs Continuing: Mathematical decision matrix using Excel XIRR to ditch a toxic endowment policy in the 4th year.

Life Insurance Corporation (LIC) agent rebating: Agents illegally passing back 50% of their first-year commission to customer as discount (Prohibited under Sec 41).

Online term insurance vs Offline term insurance: Pricing discrepancy is purely the 30% direct channel agent commission savings passed to customer.

E-KYC and digital onboarding have eliminated medicals for term life up to 50 Lakhs for standard age/income profiles (Straight Through Processing - STP).

Tele-MER (Medical Examination Report) audio/video recording legally binds the customer to non-disclosure in case of future claim dispute.

Propensity to pay models: Insurers using credit bureau (CIBIL) data to predict if a term plan customer will default on renewal premiums (Persistency ratio).

Mortality drag in ULIPs at older ages: As age increases, mortality charge skyrockets, eating up the fund value units faster than market returns.

Guaranteed Surrender Value (GSV) vs acquired Paid-up Value: A policy with 20-year term stopped at 3 years gives peanuts, stopped at 15 years gives 70%+.

Lapsed policy revival scheme discounts: Waiving the late payment interest (usually 9%) to boost 13th month and 61st month persistency.

Insurance Marketing Firms (IMF) vs Corporate Agent vs Individual Agent: IMFs can sell policies of 2 Life, 2 Health, and 2 General insurers.

Point of Sales Person (PoSP): Simplified license to sell basic standard products (two-wheeler, term life) with minimal training (15 hours).

Buying insurance from bank RM (Bancassurance) vs independent broker: Bank RMs hard-selling single premium toxic products for high targets.

Credit life refund: Foreclosing a 20-year home loan in 5 years, how to calculate and demand the pro-rata refund of the single premium credit life insurance.

Master policy vs Certificate of Insurance (COI): Group insurance mechanics where bank is master policyholder, borrower gets COI.

Taxation of critical illness rider payout: Lump sum received on cancer diagnosis is entirely tax-free under section 10(10D).

Double Tax Benefit: Paying mediclaim premium (80D) using a credit card that gives 2% cashback, optimizing net cash outflow.

Salary restructuring: Opting for employer-provided superannuation/annuity fund to reduce taxable salary perquisite limits.

Riders are capped at 30% of the base premium (IRDAI rule) so that the policy remains primarily a life insurance contract.

If basic life cover lapses, all attached riders (accidental, critical illness) automatically lapse and cannot be continued standalone.

Premium Reviewability: Base term insurance premium is fixed for life, but Critical Illness rider premiums can be revised by company every 3/5 years.

Term insurance with "Return of Premium" (TROP) includes the extra GST paid in the refunded amount? (No, GST and rider premiums are excluded from refund).

